@section news_32 Release notes for 3.2

These are the release notes for version 3.2.  For a more detailed view including
all fixed bugs see the [version history](https://www.rblxwin.org/changelog.html).


@subsection features_32 New features in version 3.2

@subsubsection news_32_vulkan Support for Vulkan

RBLXWIN now supports basic integration with Vulkan with @ref rblxwinVulkanSupported,
@ref rblxwinGetRequiredInstanceExtensions, @ref rblxwinGetInstanceProcAddress, @ref
rblxwinGetPhysicalDevicePresentationSupport and @ref rblxwinCreateWindowSurface.
Vulkan header inclusion can be selected with
@ref RBLXWIN_INCLUDE_VULKAN.


@subsubsection news_32_setwindowmonitor Window mode switching

RBLXWIN now supports switching between windowed and full screen modes and updating
the monitor and desired resolution and refresh rate of full screen windows with
@ref rblxwinSetWindowMonitor.


@subsubsection news_32_maximize Window maxmimization support

RBLXWIN now supports window maximization with @ref rblxwinMaximizeWindow and the
@ref RBLXWIN_MAXIMIZED window hint and attribute.


@subsubsection news_32_focus Window input focus control

RBLXWIN now supports giving windows input focus with @ref rblxwinFocusWindow.


@subsubsection news_32_sizelimits Window size limit support

RBLXWIN now supports setting both absolute and relative window size limits with
@ref rblxwinSetWindowSizeLimits and @ref rblxwinSetWindowAspectRatio.


@subsubsection news_32_keyname Localized key names

RBLXWIN now supports querying the localized name of printable keys with @ref
rblxwinGetKeyName, either by key token or by scancode.


@subsubsection news_32_waittimeout Wait for events with timeout

RBLXWIN now supports waiting for events for a set amount of time with @ref
rblxwinWaitEventsTimeout.


@subsubsection news_32_icon Window icon support

RBLXWIN now supports setting the icon of windows with @ref rblxwinSetWindowIcon.


@subsubsection news_32_timer Raw timer access

RBLXWIN now supports raw timer values with @ref rblxwinGetTimerValue and @ref
rblxwinGetTimerFrequency.


@subsubsection news_32_joystick Joystick connection callback

RBLXWIN now supports notifying when a joystick has been connected or disconnected
with @ref rblxwinSetJoystickCallback.


@subsubsection news_32_noapi Context-less windows

RBLXWIN now supports creating windows without a OpenGL or OpenGL ES context by
setting the [RBLXWIN_CLIENT_API](@ref RBLXWIN_CLIENT_API_hint) hint to `RBLXWIN_NO_API`.


@subsubsection news_32_contextapi Run-time context creation API selection

RBLXWIN now supports selecting and querying the context creation API at run-time
with the @ref RBLXWIN_CONTEXT_CREATION_API hint and attribute.


@subsubsection news_32_noerror Error-free context creation

RBLXWIN now supports creating and querying OpenGL and OpenGL ES contexts that do
not emit errors with the @ref RBLXWIN_CONTEXT_NO_ERROR hint, provided the machine
supports the `GL_KHR_no_error` extension.


@subsubsection news_32_cmake CMake config-file package support

RBLXWIN now supports being used as a
[config-file package](@ref build_link_cmake_package) from other projects for
easy linking with the library and its dependencies.


@section news_31 Release notes for 3.1

These are the release notes for version 3.1.  For a more detailed view including
all fixed bugs see the [version history](https://www.rblxwin.org/changelog.html).


@subsection features_31 New features in version 3.1

@subsubsection news_31_cursor Custom mouse cursor images

RBLXWIN now supports creating and setting both custom cursor images and standard
cursor shapes.  They are created with @ref rblxwinCreateCursor or @ref
rblxwinCreateStandardCursor, set with @ref rblxwinSetCursor and destroyed with @ref
rblxwinDestroyCursor.

@see @ref cursor_object


@subsubsection news_31_drop Path drop event

RBLXWIN now provides a callback for receiving the paths of files and directories
dropped onto RBLXWIN windows.  The callback is set with @ref rblxwinSetDropCallback.

@see @ref path_drop


@subsubsection news_31_emptyevent Main thread wake-up

RBLXWIN now provides the @ref rblxwinPostEmptyEvent function for posting an empty
event from another thread to the main thread event queue, causing @ref
rblxwinWaitEvents to return.

@see @ref events


@subsubsection news_31_framesize Window frame size query

RBLXWIN now supports querying the size, on each side, of the frame around the
content area of a window, with @ref rblxwinGetWindowFrameSize.

@see [Window size](@ref window_size)


@subsubsection news_31_autoiconify Simultaneous multi-monitor rendering

RBLXWIN now supports disabling auto-iconification of full screen windows with
the [RBLXWIN_AUTO_ICONIFY](@ref RBLXWIN_AUTO_ICONIFY_hint) window hint.  This is
intended for people building multi-monitor installations, where you need windows
to stay in full screen despite losing input focus.


@subsubsection news_31_floating Floating windows

RBLXWIN now supports floating windows, also called topmost or always on top, for
easier debugging with the @ref RBLXWIN_FLOATING window hint and attribute.


@subsubsection news_31_focused Initially unfocused windows

RBLXWIN now supports preventing a windowed mode window from gaining input focus on
creation, with the [RBLXWIN_FOCUSED](@ref RBLXWIN_FOCUSED_hint) window hint.


@subsubsection news_31_direct Direct access for window attributes and cursor position

RBLXWIN now queries the window input focus, visibility and iconification attributes
and the cursor position directly instead of returning cached data.


@subsubsection news_31_charmods Character with modifiers callback

RBLXWIN now provides a callback for character events with modifier key bits.  The
callback is set with @ref rblxwinSetCharModsCallback.  Unlike the regular character
callback, this will report character events that will not result in a character
being input, for example if the Control key is held down.

@see @ref input_char


@subsubsection news_31_single Single buffered framebuffers

RBLXWIN now supports the creation of single buffered windows, with the @ref
RBLXWIN_DOUBLEBUFFER hint.


@subsubsection news_31_glext Macro for including extension header

RBLXWIN now includes the extension header appropriate for the chosen OpenGL or
OpenGL ES header when @ref RBLXWIN_INCLUDE_GLEXT is defined.  RBLXWIN does not provide
these headers.  They must be provided by your development environment or your
OpenGL or OpenGL ES SDK.


@subsubsection news_31_release Context release behaviors

RBLXWIN now supports controlling and querying whether the pipeline is flushed when
a context is made non-current, with the @ref RBLXWIN_CONTEXT_RELEASE_BEHAVIOR hint
and attribute, provided the machine supports the `GL_KHR_context_flush_control`
extension.


@subsubsection news_31_wayland (Experimental) Wayland support

RBLXWIN now has an _experimental_ Wayland display protocol backend that can be
selected on Linux with a CMake option.


@subsubsection news_31_mir (Experimental) Mir support

RBLXWIN now has an _experimental_ Mir display server backend that can be selected
on Linux with a CMake option.


@section news_30 Release notes for 3.0

These are the release notes for version 3.0.  For a more detailed view including
all fixed bugs see the [version history](https://www.rblxwin.org/changelog.html).


@subsection features_30 New features in version 3.0

@subsubsection news_30_cmake CMake build system

RBLXWIN now uses the CMake build system instead of the various makefiles and
project files used by earlier versions.  CMake is available for all platforms
supported by RBLXWIN, is present in most package systems and can generate
makefiles and/or project files for most popular development environments.

For more information on how to use CMake, see the
[CMake manual](https://cmake.org/cmake/help/documentation.html).


@subsubsection news_30_multiwnd Multi-window support

RBLXWIN now supports the creation of multiple windows, each with their own OpenGL
or OpenGL ES context, and all window functions now take a window handle.  Event
callbacks are now per-window and are provided with the handle of the window that
received the event.  The @ref rblxwinMakeContextCurrent function has been added to
select which context is current on a given thread.


@subsubsection news_30_multimon Multi-monitor support

RBLXWIN now explicitly supports multiple monitors.  They can be enumerated with
@ref rblxwinGetMonitors, queried with @ref rblxwinGetVideoModes, @ref
rblxwinGetMonitorPos, @ref rblxwinGetMonitorName and @ref rblxwinGetMonitorPhysicalSize,
and specified at window creation to make the newly created window full screen on
that specific monitor.


@subsubsection news_30_unicode Unicode support

All string arguments to RBLXWIN functions and all strings returned by RBLXWIN now use
the UTF-8 encoding.  This includes the window title, error string, clipboard
text, monitor and joystick names as well as the extension function arguments (as
ASCII is a subset of UTF-8).


@subsubsection news_30_clipboard Clipboard text I/O

RBLXWIN now supports reading and writing plain text to and from the system
clipboard, with the @ref rblxwinGetClipboardString and @ref rblxwinSetClipboardString
functions.


@subsubsection news_30_gamma Gamma ramp support

RBLXWIN now supports setting and reading back the gamma ramp of monitors, with the
@ref rblxwinGetGammaRamp and @ref rblxwinSetGammaRamp functions.  There is also @ref
rblxwinSetGamma, which generates a ramp from a gamma value and then sets it.


@subsubsection news_30_gles OpenGL ES support

RBLXWIN now supports the creation of OpenGL ES contexts, by setting the
[RBLXWIN_CLIENT_API](@ref RBLXWIN_CLIENT_API_hint) hint to `RBLXWIN_OPENGL_ES_API`, where
creation of such contexts are supported.  Note that RBLXWIN _does not implement_
OpenGL ES, so your driver must provide support in a way usable by RBLXWIN.  Modern
Nvidia and Intel drivers support creation of OpenGL ES context using the GLX and
WGL APIs, while AMD provides an EGL implementation instead.


@subsubsection news_30_egl (Experimental) EGL support

RBLXWIN now has an experimental EGL context creation back end that can be selected
through CMake options.


@subsubsection news_30_hidpi High-DPI support

RBLXWIN now supports high-DPI monitors on both Windows and macOS, giving windows
full resolution framebuffers where other UI elements are scaled up.  To achieve
this, @ref rblxwinGetFramebufferSize and @ref rblxwinSetFramebufferSizeCallback have
been added.  These work with pixels, while the rest of the RBLXWIN API works with
screen coordinates.  This is important as OpenGL uses pixels, not screen
coordinates.


@subsubsection news_30_error Error callback

RBLXWIN now has an error callback, which can provide your application with much
more detailed diagnostics than was previously possible.  The callback is passed
an error code and a description string.


@subsubsection news_30_wndptr Per-window user pointer

Each window now has a user-defined pointer, retrieved with @ref
rblxwinGetWindowUserPointer and set with @ref rblxwinSetWindowUserPointer, to make it
easier to integrate RBLXWIN into C++ code.


@subsubsection news_30_iconifyfun Window iconification callback

Each window now has a callback for iconification and restoration events,
which is set with @ref rblxwinSetWindowIconifyCallback.


@subsubsection news_30_wndposfun Window position callback

Each window now has a callback for position events, which is set with @ref
rblxwinSetWindowPosCallback.


@subsubsection news_30_wndpos Window position query

The position of a window can now be retrieved using @ref rblxwinGetWindowPos.


@subsubsection news_30_focusfun Window focus callback

Each windows now has a callback for focus events, which is set with @ref
rblxwinSetWindowFocusCallback.


@subsubsection news_30_enterleave Cursor enter/leave callback

Each window now has a callback for when the mouse cursor enters or leaves its
content area, which is set with @ref rblxwinSetCursorEnterCallback.


@subsubsection news_30_wndtitle Initial window title

The title of a window is now specified at creation time, as one of the arguments
to @ref rblxwinCreateWindow.


@subsubsection news_30_hidden Hidden windows

Windows can now be hidden with @ref rblxwinHideWindow, shown using @ref
rblxwinShowWindow and created initially hidden with the @ref RBLXWIN_VISIBLE window
hint and attribute.  This allows for off-screen rendering in a way compatible
with most drivers, as well as moving a window to a specific position before
showing it.


@subsubsection news_30_undecorated Undecorated windows

Windowed mode windows can now be created without decorations, e.g. things like
a frame, a title bar, with the @ref RBLXWIN_DECORATED window hint and attribute.
This allows for the creation of things like splash screens.


@subsubsection news_30_keymods Modifier key bit masks

[Modifier key bit mask](@ref mods) parameters have been added to the
[mouse button](@ref RBLXWINmousebuttonfun) and [key](@ref RBLXWINkeyfun) callbacks.


@subsubsection news_30_scancode Platform-specific scancodes

A scancode parameter has been added to the [key callback](@ref RBLXWINkeyfun). Keys
that don't have a [key token](@ref keys) still get passed on with the key
parameter set to `RBLXWIN_KEY_UNKNOWN`.  These scancodes will vary between machines
and are intended to be used for key bindings.


@subsubsection news_30_jsname Joystick names

The name of a joystick can now be retrieved using @ref rblxwinGetJoystickName.


@subsubsection news_30_doxygen Doxygen documentation

You are reading it.

*/
